{number: 107}
{title: Abide with Me}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
A-[C] bide with [G7] me: fast [C] falls the [F] eventide;
The [C] darkness [Am] deepens; [D7] Lord, with me a-[G7] bide:
When [C] other [G7] helpers [C] fail and [F] comforts flee,
Help [C] of the [Am] helpless, [C] O a-[G7] bide with [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
Swift [C] to its [G7] close ebbs [C] out life's [F] little day;
Earth's [C] joys grow [Am] dim, its [D7] glories pass a-[G7] way;
Change [C] and de-[G7] cay in [C] all a-[F] round I see;
O [C] Thou who [Am] changest not, [C] a-[G7] bide with [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
I [C] need Thy [G7] presence [C] every [F] passing hour;
What [C] but Thy [Am] grace can [D7] foil the tempter's [G7] pow'r?
Who, [C] like Thy-[G7] self, my [C] guide and [F] stay can be?
Through [C] cloud and [Am] sunshine, [C] Lord, a-[G7] bide with [C] me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
Hold [C] Thou Thy [G7] cross be-[C] fore my [F] closing eyes;
Shine [C] through the [Am] gloom and [D7] point me to the [G7] skies:
Heav'n's [C] morning [G7] breaks, and [C] earth's vain [F] shadows flee;
In [C] life, in [Am] death, O [C] Lord, a-[G7] bide with [C] me.
{end_of_verse}
